      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sweet Valley’s name honors Ross Township, which was formed in January 1842 from parts of Union and Lehman townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sweet_valley_pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area was originally part of Lenape territory, whose Algonquian‑speaking people farmed, hunted, and fished in the fertile valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sweet_valley_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 30‑acre Harris Pond nearby offers fishing for largemouth bass, sunfish, bluegills, and perch, stocked by the Pennsylvania Fish and Boat Commission.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
